{"content":[{"c":["BRIBE, BRIBERY"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["To give a person in authority something valuable in order to influence that person’s decision or action. Bribery was prohibited under OT law (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.23.8","r":"Exod.23.8","rawR":"Exod.23.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.23.8","value":"Exod.23.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 23:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.16.19","r":"Deut.16.19","rawR":"Deut.16.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.16.19","value":"Deut.16.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 16:19"},") and condemned by the prophets (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.1.23","r":"Isa.1.23","rawR":"Isa.1.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.1.23","value":"Isa.1.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 1:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.5.12","r":"Amos.5.12","rawR":"Amos.5.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.5.12","value":"Amos.5.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 5:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.3.11","r":"Mic.3.11","rawR":"Mic.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.3.11","value":"Mic.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 3:11"},"). Although Samuel denied that he ever took a bribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.12.3","r":"1Sam.12.3","rawR":"1Sam.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.12.3","value":"1Sam.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 12:3"},"), his sons did not maintain the same standard (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.8.3","r":"1Sam.8.3","rawR":"1Sam.8.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.8.3","value":"1Sam.8.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The distinction between bribery and merely giving gifts was not always clear. Hence, giving something valuable is seen as a way to prevent unwanted conflict (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.21.14","r":"Pr.21.14","rawR":"Pr.21.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.21.14","value":"Pr.21.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 21:14"},"). Giving a gift is described (with neither approval nor condemnation) as a way to get ahead (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.18.16","r":"Pr.18.16","rawR":"Pr.18.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.18.16","value":"Pr.18.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["For the most part, bribery is seen in the Bible as despicable. “The wicked accept secret bribes to pervert justice” (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.17.23","r":"Pr.17.23","rawR":"Pr.17.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.17.23","value":"Pr.17.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 17:23"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Any system that legitimizes bribery gives the rich an unfair advantage in persuading leaders and judges; the poor find it difficult to get a fair hearing. Innocent people who are poor can be condemned; guilty people who are rich can offer a sizable bribe and go free (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.15.5","r":"Ps.15.5","rawR":"Ps.15.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.15.5","value":"Ps.15.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 15:5b"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.5.23","r":"Isa.5.23","rawR":"Isa.5.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.5.23","value":"Isa.5.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 5:23"},"). In extreme cases, bribes are said to have been used to hire killers (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.27.25","r":"Deut.27.25","rawR":"Deut.27.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.27.25","value":"Deut.27.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 27:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.22.12","r":"Ezek.22.12","rawR":"Ezek.22.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.22.12","value":"Ezek.22.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 22:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BribeBribery","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 23:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.23.8","rawQueryValue":"Exod.23.8","sourceRefExact":"Exod.23.8"},{"anchorText":"Dt 16:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.16.19","rawQueryValue":"Deut.16.19","sourceRefExact":"Deut.16.19"},{"anchorText":"Is 1:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.1.23","rawQueryValue":"Isa.1.23","sourceRefExact":"Isa.1.23"},{"anchorText":"Am 5:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.5.12","rawQueryValue":"Amos.5.12","sourceRefExact":"Amos.5.12"},{"anchorText":"Mi 3:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.3.11","rawQueryValue":"Mic.3.11","sourceRefExact":"Mic.3.11"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.12.3","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.12.3","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.12.3"},{"anchorText":"8:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.8.3","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.8.3","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.8.3"},{"anchorText":"Prv 21:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.21.14","rawQueryValue":"Pr.21.14","sourceRefExact":"Pr.21.14"},{"anchorText":"18:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.18.16","rawQueryValue":"Pr.18.16","sourceRefExact":"Pr.18.16"},{"anchorText":"Prv 17:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.17.23","rawQueryValue":"Pr.17.23","sourceRefExact":"Pr.17.23"},{"anchorText":"Ps 15:5b","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.15.5","rawQueryValue":"Ps.15.5","sourceRefExact":"Ps.15.5"},{"anchorText":"Is 5:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.5.23","rawQueryValue":"Isa.5.23","sourceRefExact":"Isa.5.23"},{"anchorText":"Dt 27:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.27.25","rawQueryValue":"Deut.27.25","sourceRefExact":"Deut.27.25"},{"anchorText":"Ez 22:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.22.12","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.22.12","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.22.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a007320d082ac4b7218291210bee5dfd9f87c90b838a146210ab11322e5d95cb","sourceItemName":"BribeBribery","sourceItemOrder":409,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BribeBribery","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bribe, Bribery","title":"Bribe, Bribery","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}